<title>UK: Glaxo Wellcome to boost genetics research.</title>
<headline>Glaxo Wellcome to boost genetics research.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>British drugs giant Glaxo Wellcome Plc said on Tuesday it created a Genetics Directorate to boost its research and development in the field of genetics.</p>
<p>With a budget of over 30 million stg for 1997, the directorate will stand alongside existing R&amp;D groups and cover clinical, development and commercial aspects of genetics, as well as existing research programmes.</p>
<p>The company expected to double staff numbers at the group over the next 18 months.</p>
<p>The directorate had about 150 researchers working in Britain, the U.S. and Switzerland.</p>
<p>&quot;We believe we have brought together an unrivalled combination of people and technologies that will continue our good progress towards the goal of three significant new medicines a year by the year 2000,&quot; Glaxo said in a statement.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
